      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was the cause of the unexpected gold diffs in the first CL, *after* I had updated it to use a bool to track presence of the join control point.\n\nIn the original original, which did not cause diffs, when there was no prior join point, writeCircle would just automatically reset the attrib to something with nans in it, and the correct state of no join point would be restored. After switching to using a boolean, updateJoinControlPointAttrib() always marked the bool as true, so even if we set the point back to it\u0027s prior state after writing the circle patch, the writer would think we\u0027d have join info when we shouldn\u0027t have. This leads to bad stroke joins.",
